WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.849
Welcome to Grade 3 English, Unit 5: Actions and Activities.

2
00:00:03.929 --> 00:00:09.575
You will learn thirteen action words,
including build, discuss, protect and celebrate.

3
00:00:09.655 --> 00:00:16.500
You will talk about what you did using the past
simple, explain reasons and results with because and so,

4
00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:22.893
order events with First, Next, Then and Finally,
ask Wh- questions, and share opinions politely.

5
00:00:22.973 --> 00:00:30.750
The unit story, “The Wall Behind the Garden”, follows Amal,
Leo and their class as they build a reading wall together.

6
00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:36.344
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

7
00:00:36.424 --> 00:00:43.571
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name
and use many action words, such as build, listen,

8
00:00:43.651 --> 00:00:45.177
protect and celebrate.

9
00:00:45.257 --> 00:00:51.967
You will also talk about things you did, using
the past simple (built, listened, celebrated).

10
00:00:52.047 --> 00:00:56.858
You will also explain why something
happened, using because and so.

11
00:00:56.938 --> 00:00:59.559
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

12
00:00:59.639 --> 00:01:05.408
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
discuss, listen, offer, build, complete, remove.

13
00:01:05.488 --> 00:01:10.448
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

14
00:01:10.528 --> 00:01:14.369
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

15
00:01:14.449 --> 00:01:18.115
The reading sequence includes A
Busy Saturday and Helping Hands.

16
00:01:18.195 --> 00:01:18.934
Read actively.

17
00:01:19.014 --> 00:01:22.972
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

18
00:01:23.052 --> 00:01:26.777
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

19
00:01:26.857 --> 00:01:30.337
The first language focus is The Past Simple Tense.

20
00:01:30.417 --> 00:01:36.318
We use the past simple to talk about actions
that already happened and are finished.

21
00:01:36.398 --> 00:01:40.092
It helps us tell stories and share the things we did.

22
00:01:40.172 --> 00:01:45.433
In this unit's story the children built
a wall, so we say built, not build.

23
00:01:45.513 --> 00:01:53.194
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

24
00:01:53.274 --> 00:01:57.348
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 — Tell What You Did.

25
00:01:57.428 --> 00:02:01.837
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

26
00:02:01.917 --> 00:02:05.253
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

27
00:02:05.333 --> 00:02:08.804
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

28
00:02:08.884 --> 00:02:10.377
You are ready to begin.

29
00:02:10.457 --> 00:02:17.146
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

30
00:02:17.226 --> 00:02:20.428
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

31
00:02:20.508 --> 00:02:28.017
Use AI English for hints and feedback any time, and bring
your questions to a live session too if you join one.
